Players: [Merchants]; Strategies: [Haggle (proportion p), Fair Trade (proportion 1-p)];
Profit functions: E(H)=5-7p, E(F)=3-3p;
Average profit: \bar{f}=p·E(H)+(1-p)·E(F);
Replicator equation for Haggle: dp/dt = p (E(H)-\bar{f});
Equilibrium when E(H)=E(F) → 5-7p = 3-3p → p* = 0.5; Stability: if p>0.5, E(F)>E(H) → p decreases; if p<0.5, E(H)>E(F) → p increases.

Players: [Farmer A, Farmer B]; Strategies: [Tit‑for‑Tat (TFT), All‑Defect (AllD), All‑Cooperate (AllC), Grim‑Trigger]; Payoffs per round: (C,C)=(3,3), (C,D)=(0,5), (D,C)=(5,0), (D,D)=(1,1);
TFT vs TFT over n rounds: each receives 3n;
TFT vs AllD: round 1 → (0,5), rounds 2‑n → (1,1) each;
Cooperation is a subgame‑perfect equilibrium when discount factor δ > (T‑R)/(T‑P) = (5‑3)/(5‑1) = 0.5.

Players: [Attacker, Defender];
Strategies: Attacker=[Attack, Wait], Defender=[Reinforce, Sally];
Payoffs: (Wait)=(1,2), (Attack, Reinforce)=(2,3), (Attack,Sally)=(4,0);
Backward induction steps:
1) Defender node after Attack: Reinforce (3) > Sally (0).
2) Attacker node: Attack (2) > Wait (1).
SPE: (Attack, Reinforce) with payoffs (2,3).

